{
  "systemPrompt": "Assume you are a senior HR professional with 10+ years of experience in IT support and help desk hiring.",
  "userPrompt": "Task:\nWrite the **CV Summary section** — the single paragraph that appears at the top of the resume, directly under the candidate's name and contact details, and above the Professional Experience section. This is the named \"Summary\" (or \"Professional Summary\") block that recruiters read first.\n\nImportant: This is NOT a simple recap or compression of the experience bullets below. It is an opening pitch: a short, role-specific hook that answers \"why this person fits this role\" before the reader sees the detailed experience. Do not merely list or summarise past roles; craft a cohesive paragraph that highlights fit with the JD and (when provided) the company.\n\nVoice (strict — this text sits on the candidate's own CV):\n- Write as CV-ready copy the candidate would put under their own name — NOT as a referral, nomination, placement blurb, or third-party recommendation\n- Do NOT use \"this candidate\", \"the candidate\", \"Selected for…\", \"chosen for…\", \"pathway\", \"placement program\", or similar framing\n- Prefer implied third person without naming the person (e.g. start from role/stack/capability: \"IT support professional with…\" / \"Help desk specialist experienced in…\")\n- No first-person \"I\"; no motivational or career-counsellor phrasing\n\nRequirements:\n- Length: target ~50 words (hard max 60). Prefer 2 short sentences over one dense sentence\n- Paragraph must be coherent; no more than 3 items in any parallel list\n- Company alignment (when company profile is provided): weave in ONE light, concrete hook — domain, product type, or tools the company uses — not a name-drop sandwich. Do NOT force company mentions into both the first and last sentence. When company profile is empty (JD-only), base the summary only on the JD\n- Match the tone and structure of a professional Australian IT support resume\n- Avoid buzzwords, clichés, and soft-skill fillers (e.g. \"agile environments\", \"team player\", \"passionate\", \"eager to grow\", \"customer-focused mindset\")\n\nContent constraints:\n- Base the summary strictly on the candidate information in the mapping below (CANDIDATE SUMMARY and MAPPING sections)\n- Prefer JD-relevant transferable capabilities evidenced in the mapping (triage, access, documentation, escalation, reliability). Name a JD tool/platform ONLY if the mapping evidence includes it — do NOT invent Microsoft 365 / Active Directory / Service Desk / Azure hands-on experience\n- A few high-signal evidenced matches are enough; not a ticket/project laundry list\n- Do NOT use generic phrases that could apply to any IT support candidate\n- Do NOT introduce new skills, tools, or responsibilities\n- Do NOT exaggerate scope, seniority, or impact\n- Do NOT simply repeat or condense the experience bullets; the Summary is a high-level pitch, not a list of tickets or deliverables\n- Do NOT invent hyphenated coinages or role-reframe labels (e.g. \"support-style\", \"IT support–oriented\", \"SLA-style\", \"incident-style\", \"queue-style\", \"MSP-style\")\n- Do NOT close with aspiration, fit-rating, or application meta. Banned endings include: \"well aligned to…\", \"well suited to…\", \"strong fit for…\", \"ideal for…\", \"ready to join…\", \"seeking a … role at…\", \"global … partner\"\n- End on a concrete evidenced capability or domain hook, not a verdict about role fit\n- Do NOT reframe training, bootcamp, or partner pathways as the headline of the summary; if relevant at all, at most one short factual credential — capability and JD fit come first\n\nIntent:\n- The summary should quickly communicate how the person's experience directly matches the job requirements\n- It should function as a hook that shows immediate relevance to the role\n- Prioritize JD-specific alignment over generic professional description or company-marketing language\n\nCompany profile (company-specific context; leave empty if none):\n{{companyProfile}}\n\nJob Description:\n{{jd}}\n\nKey Hiring Pain Points:\n{{painPoints}}\n\nMapping (use CANDIDATE SUMMARY and MAPPING sections as the only candidate context):\n{{mapping}}\n\nWrite your response in plain text format in English. Do NOT use JSON format. Write one coherent paragraph (~50 words, max 60). CV-ready voice only; light company domain/tech fit when a profile is provided; otherwise JD-only.",
  "temperature": 0.7,
  "maxTokens": 500
}
